hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27686","Haddathana Haytham, meaning Ibn Kharijah, he said: Haddathana Hafs ibn Maysarah, from Ibn Harmalah, from Abu Thifal al-Murri, that he said: I heard Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Huwaytib saying: My grandmother narrated to me that she heard her father saying: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There is no prayer for one who has no ablution, no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it, and he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and he does not believe in me who does not love the Ansar."
"27687","Haddathana Yunus: Haddathana Abu Ma'shar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Abu Thifal al-Murri, from Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Huwaytib, from his grandmother, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: He does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and he does not believe in me who does not love the Ansar, and there is no prayer for one who has no ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it."
"27688","Haddathana Affan, he said: Haddathana Wuhayb, he said: Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, that he heard Abu Thifal narrating, saying: I heard Rabah ibn Abd al-Rahman, and Affan once did not say: Ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Huwaytib, saying: My grandmother narrated to me that she heard her father saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There is no prayer for one who has no ablution, no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it, and he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and he does not believe in me who does not love the Ansar."
